Z||000026||Cozmo||05-25-2001||07:33 AM||||Hard to say...<BR>Having 2 notchbacks and a newly acquired fastback, I tend to be more fond of the notchback body.  It's unique silhouette is instantly recognizable as "Fiero"; whereas the fastback has a more conventional outline.<BR>   Some of my "non-Fiero" friends (yeah, I'm working on them <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) say the fastback looks larger and meaner (some even say "pregnant").<BR>   When you're in the drivers' seat tho the only difference is rearward visibility (or lack of it...)<BR>I love tough choices... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B>C02M0</B><BR><I>Suncoast Fieros</I><BR>'85 silver 2M6 4spd. Targa <B>"Silver Streak"</B><BR>'86 black auto GT <B>"Blackbird"</B><BR>'87 white auto Coupe <B>"The Duke"</B>||||reg||14
Z||000027||FieroHeather||05-25-2001||08:24 AM||||Both types of backs are great.  My first encounter with a Fiero was an '85 notchback.  That car was sweet--then I met up with like the GTA club for a run down to Cayauga and found out that Fieros actually come in different shapes and sizes (relatively speaking)!  I still have a special place for the notchback, but I think I like the curves of the fastback better  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Looks more aerodynamic.||||reg||14
Z||000028||ChadMan||05-25-2001||08:56 AM||||I can't decide the answer to this any more than I can decide the answer to the classic question "Ginger or Mary Ann"?  They're both beautiful and appealing, but in different ways.<P>I've never had a fastback, though.  Guess I'm a Mary Ann kind of guy.||||reg||12
Z||000029||stsmithgt||05-25-2001||09:41 AM||||I'm hooked on fastbacks.  All kinds of fastbacks.  Most of the cars I've own have been that way.  The knotchback has a very individual look while the fastback is unique.  It's in the eye of the owner who can find what they like most in the car.  So what ever floats your boat....Bad metafore.  What ever puts wind in your sail(panel) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> So be it.<P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
